        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.case.edu/EpilepsyOntology.owl#EpileptiformBenignVariant"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Breach rhythm refers to high-voltage activity that occurs in the region of a skull defect and have a spiky appearance and consist of sharply contoured arciform waveforms that usually have a frequency of 6-11 Hz.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Breach Rhythm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


