        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.case.edu/EpilepsyOntology.owl#MotorSeizure"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Complex motor seizures consist of motor seizures during which the patient performs movements that imitate natural movements, are relatively complex, and tend to involve different body segments, which are moved in different planes.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Motor (mapping reference: ILAE 2017 Classification of Seizure Types Expanded Version)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Complex Motor Seizure</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


