        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.case.edu/EpilepsyOntology.owl#FaceSubdivision"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The proximal portion of the digestive tract, containing the oral cavity and bounded by the oral opening. In vertebrates, this extends to the pharynx and includes teeth, gums, lips, tongue and parts of the palate</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>http://sig.uw.edu/fma#Mouth</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


