        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.case.edu/EpilepsyOntology.owl#InterIctalPattern"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Sharp waves that are focal or hemispheric in distribution and occur in a periodic or semi-periodic fashion. They are called bi-PLEDs when they occur in both hemispheres but do so asynchronously between the two hemispheres</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Periodic Lateralized Epileptiform Discharge (PLED)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


